    rock--Sela, that is, Petra, the metropolis of Idumea and the Nabathoean Ishmaelites. Or it may refer in general to those in Arabia-Petraea, who had their dwellings cut out of the rock. 

    the mountains--namely, of Paran, south of Sinai, in Arabic Petraea [VITRINGA].

